            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Karen Dee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This would be a four-star rating if it weren't for the garlic in the recipe. The flavor of the garlic masked the basic ham flavor, as well as the wonderful mango chutney and Dijon. It's too overpowering and should either be reduced to ONE clove, or eliminated entirely."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Molly"
            },
            "reviewBody": "A delicious glaze that I've made twice. The first time I used orange marmalade in place of the mango chutney, the second time I used apricot jam as that is what I had on hand. The mixture of the brown sugar, orange juice, mustard, garlic and marmalade/jam was equally delicious. I have another ham in the freezer and I look forward to making this recipe again. Served the ham with 'Mom's Scalloped Potatoes' from AR.",
            "datePublished": "2015-02-28T20:07:13.570Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kim McCarthy Bond"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made it exactly according to the recipe and it was great! I do NOT understand how people can rate a recipe that they have changed, especially when it's the main ingredient that they change. If you did NOT use Mango Chutney, then you did NOT make THIS recipe people. After I made it per the recipe I did make a change or two, such as substituting POG for OJ because it's what I had, and I added maraschino cherries because of a special request, and it came out great. But my rating is for the recipe as written.",
            "datePublished": "2015-04-03T18:05:19.273Z"
          },
          {
